# The M2 ritual ledger — one line per ritual, appended by
# `cargo xtask bench ritual` (lines starting with `#` are this header).
#
# THE TICK RULE (s44: "three consecutive nightly runs"): `consecutive`
# is 0 after any DOES-NOT-HOLD; a HOLDS advances the previous count by
# one ONLY when >= 12 hours separate it from the previously COUNTED
# hold — two samples of one thermal state are one tick, however many
# timestamps they wear. A closer HOLDS is recorded with the count
# unchanged and a note. At consecutive >= 3 the tool prints the
# declaration-threshold banner; the declaration itself is the human's.
#
# Lines 1-9 are the hand-runs (2026-08-20 -> -22, #89), backfilled from
# their conditions files' own UTC stamps. Note what the honest stamps
# say: runs 8 and 9 are EIGHTEEN MINUTES apart — the local calendar
# rolled over between them, but a night did not pass. Run 9 is
# therefore recorded as a same-night re-render and the tail count is 1,
# not the 2 the run-9 publication claimed. The instrument outvotes the
# narrative, here as everywhere.
